            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Mandarin for in large amounts, then the Mandarin for a small amount of."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: xiàdān",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "xiàdān — \"to place an order\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "wǒ xiàdān yǐjīng sān tiān le dōngxi hái méi dào — I placed the order three days ago, and it still hasn't arrived."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Its characters come later; for now it is a word for the ear."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "xiàdān is built from 下 'to put down' and dān 'a slip of paper', both inherited from Middle Chinese, haeX and tan (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), which glosses the first 'to go down' and the second 'single'; the sense 'an order slip' is modern."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying how it was."
            }
          ]
        },
